;; Usage: nelisp --load test/standalone-string-to-number-check.el
;;
;; A float went through an interpreted digit walk, about 1 ms per number,
;; and SVG/DXF parsing is mostly floats.  A whole float literal now takes
;; the native fast path (Clinger: an exact mantissa and power of ten, one
;; IEEE operation) or the reader's exact converter.  Every value below is
;; what GNU Emacs 31.1 answers: edge cases (subnormals, 17+ digits,
;; overflow, partial tokens, leading dots, whitespace) and 900 random
;; floats in repr, fixed and exponent forms.  The "1.0e+INF" / "NaN" forms
;; are left out: the walk still reads them as 1.0, a known gap.  Prints
;; one STRING-TO-NUMBER line and exits non-zero on failure.

